---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import AirTimeHeader from '../../components/AirTimeHeader.astro';
import AirTimeFooter from '../../components/AirTimeFooter.astro';
import '../../styles/airtime.css';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="AirTime Support"
			description="Help and contact for the AirTime iPhone app by Coobeeyon Development."
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="airtime">
		<AirTimeHeader />

		<main>
			<h1>AirTime Support</h1>

			<hr />

			<p>
				AirTime shows the shape of a conversation (who spoke when and for how long)
				without keeping or showing what was said. Analysis runs on your iPhone.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Email <a href="mailto:mike.daum@coobeeyon.net">mike.daum@coobeeyon.net</a>.
				Please don't send recordings unless everyone in them has agreed.
			</p>

			<h2>Common questions</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>How does the free conversation work?</strong> Your first conversation,
				up to 5 minutes, is free. It only counts once a result with detected speech is
				saved, so failed, cancelled or silent attempts don't use it up.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>What does the subscription include?</strong> Unlimited conversations,
				each up to 30 minutes. Eligible new subscribers may get a 7-day free trial.
				Your saved conversations stay available if the subscription ends.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>How do I cancel or restore?</strong> Manage or cancel in your Apple
				Account's subscription settings, or from AirTime's subscription screen. To
				restore on a new iPhone, tap Restore Purchases there. Restoring returns access,
				not conversations: they stay on the iPhone that recorded them.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Why are the results different from what I expected?</strong> All
				results are estimates. Similar voices, background noise, short turns and people
				far from the phone can be misattributed. Overlap is time when two voices were
				detected together; it isn't proof of an interruption.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Does it work offline?</strong> Yes. Recording and analysis work in
				airplane mode. Buying or restoring a subscription needs a connection.
			</p>

			<p>
				<a href="/airtime/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> ·
				<a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">Terms of Use (Apple standard EULA)</a>
			</p>
		</main>

		<AirTimeFooter />
	</body>
</html>
